  "slug": "phylogenetic-scalable-0e43",
  "summary": "Recent preprints audit leakage, saliency validity, and statistical testing in biological prediction and screening models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is validation rigor in computational biology models, where evaluation procedures rather than model architecture are the object of scrutiny. A counterfactual perturbation protocol tests whether saliency maps in siRNA efficacy prediction reflect genuine sequence determinants, revealing cross-dataset failure modes. An audit of cancer drug response prediction finds that pre-cross-validation feature screening leaks information and inflates error, with leakage present in 23 of 32 audited published methods. Separately, SIR applies nonparametric two-dimensional isotonic regression with wild-bootstrap p-values to drug synergy matrices, reporting higher replicate concordance. GRAPE applies regression to detect genetic interactions in combinatorial CRISPR screens and is validated with the Synulator simulation pipeline. What is new is explicit, quantitative testing of evaluation validity across these works.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-02-14"
}
